course: dictionary
lesson: 3790
title: Footsteps: a step, a sound, a path
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Footstep can mean one step that someone takes when walking, or the sound that step makes. Read the sentence to see which one fits. «I heard footsteps behind me» is about sound, because you can hear them.
explain: Some words sit inside a phrase, and the phrase means something different from the single words. «Follow in someone's footsteps» does not mean walking behind a person. It means doing the same thing they did, such as the same job. «She followed in her mother's footsteps» means she copied the path her mum took in life.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «In a nature film a tiny ant marches across a leaf with loud crunchy footsteps.» An ant cannot make one step that is loud and crunchy, so here footsteps means the sounds the ant makes as it walks.
fact: A footstep is one step that someone takes when walking.
fact: A footstep can also be the sound of a step, as in «I heard footsteps behind me.»
fact: «Follow in someone's footsteps» means do the same thing they did, such as the same job.
fact: Foley artists make footsteps and rustling sounds in a studio, and match them to the film.
fact: «Yī èr sān mùtourén!» is Grandma's footsteps: move after «mùtourén» and you're out.
exercise: «I heard footsteps behind me in the dark.» What are footsteps here? | A leaf | A kind of game | *The sound of steps | A pair of shoes
exercise: Mia wants to follow in her grandad's footsteps as a doctor. What does that mean? | Walk behind him on the path | Buy the same shoes | *Do the same job he did | Stop walking
exercise: «The ant made one tiny footstep on the leaf.» What is one footstep? | A big jump | *One step that someone takes | A kind of shoe | The sound of a whole song
test: In «Foley artists stomp on gravel to make footsteps», what does footsteps mean? | *The sounds of steps | A stone | A walk in the park | A pair of boots
test: «Follow in someone's footsteps» means what? | Tread on their feet | Wait for them to stop | *Do the same thing they did | Walk in the same place as them at the same time
exam: Jun wants to be a pilot like his dad, so he will follow in his footsteps. What does this mean? | Wear his dad's shoes | *Copy his dad's path and become a pilot | Walk through the airport with him | Wait at the airport for him
